[["page","lines",0],{"text":"JOURNAL OF PLASTIC SURGERY AND HAND SURGERY 69","fontSize":7.5,"x":388.2394,"y":25.500200000000063,"width":179.21250000000003,"height":7.5}]
[["page","lines",1],{"text":"The change for baseline versus 24 in the intervention group was 32.8","fontSize":9,"x":42,"y":259.5268,"width":256.707,"height":9}]
[["page","lines",2],{"text":"(95% CI 18.9 to 46.7) and for the controls 11.1 units (95% CI 3.9 to","fontSize":9,"x":42,"y":270.83979999999997,"width":256.72770000000025,"height":9}]
[["page","lines",3],{"text":"18.4). Physical well-being chest: Change was shown neither between","fontSize":9,"x":42,"y":282.15279999999996,"width":256.752,"height":9}]
[["page","lines",4],{"text":"the groups nor over time within the groups (Table 5).","fontSize":9,"x":42,"y":293.46579999999994,"width":197.33399999999992,"height":9}]
[["page","lines",5],{"text":"Patient-related outcome – Satisfaction: Satisfaction of outcome:","fontSize":9,"x":54.006,"y":304.77879999999993,"width":244.71720000000002,"height":9}]
[["page","lines",6],{"text":"There was a ‘little’ difference after 6 months, 5.1 (95% CI –9.7 to 19.9),","fontSize":9,"x":42.009,"y":316.0917999999999,"width":256.69890000000015,"height":9}]
[["page","lines",7],{"text":"after 24 months it was ‘moderate’, 13.2 (95% CI –2.8 to 29.1), although","fontSize":9,"x":42.009,"y":327.4047999999999,"width":256.7610000000001,"height":9}]
[["page","lines",8],{"text":"one of them significant. Comparing 6 versus 24 showed no difference","fontSize":9,"x":42.009,"y":338.7177999999999,"width":256.71510000000006,"height":9}]
[["page","lines",9],{"text":"in the intervention group but the controls showed a ‘little’ decline,","fontSize":9,"x":42.009,"y":350.0307999999999,"width":256.7151,"height":9}]
[["page","lines",10],{"text":"-8.5 (95% CI –15.7 to 1.3). Satisfaction with the breast: There was No","fontSize":9,"x":42.009,"y":361.3437999999999,"width":256.69980000000015,"height":9}]
[["page","lines",11],{"text":"difference between the groups at baseline, –2.1 (95% CI –10.4 to 6.2).","fontSize":9,"x":42.009,"y":372.65679999999986,"width":256.7502000000001,"height":9}]
[["page","lines",12],{"text":"After 24 months the difference was ‘moderate’ 12.54 (95% CI 2.66 to","fontSize":9,"x":42.009,"y":383.96979999999985,"width":256.73220000000026,"height":9}]
[["page","lines",13],{"text":"22.43). In baseline versus 6 AFT had a ‘moderate’ change and the","fontSize":9,"x":42.009,"y":395.28279999999984,"width":256.6998000000001,"height":9}]
[["page","lines",14],{"text":"controls had a ‘little’ change that persisted in baseline versus 24","fontSize":9,"x":42.009,"y":406.5957999999998,"width":256.75020000000023,"height":9}]
[["page","lines",15],{"text":"months 9.25 (95% CI 2.63 to 15.87). The intervention group had a ‘very","fontSize":9,"x":42.009,"y":417.9087999999998,"width":256.70340000000016,"height":9}]
[["page","lines",16],{"text":"much’ change in baseline versus 24, 21.33 (95% CI 11.92 to 30.75).","fontSize":9,"x":42.009,"y":429.2217999999998,"width":256.7511000000002,"height":9}]
[["page","lines",17],{"text":"Satisfaction with breast nipples after 24 months showed a non-","fontSize":9,"x":42.009,"y":440.5347999999998,"width":256.75020000000006,"height":9}]
[["page","lines",18],{"text":"significant difference of 14.9 (95% CI –3.8 to 33.6) between the groups","fontSize":9,"x":310.731,"y":259.53579999999977,"width":256.6971,"height":9}]
[["page","lines",19],{"text":"(Table 6). There were no differences in satisfaction with nipples,","fontSize":9,"x":310.731,"y":270.5337999999998,"width":256.7231999999999,"height":9}]
[["page","lines",20],{"text":"surgeon, medical team, and information between the groups.","fontSize":9,"x":310.731,"y":281.53179999999975,"width":229.58640000000014,"height":9.000000000000057}]
[["page","lines",21],{"text":"Harms: One patient had a pneumothorax that was conservatively","fontSize":9,"x":322.728,"y":292.5297999999998,"width":244.69830000000007,"height":9}]
[["page","lines",22],{"text":"treated, and one had a laryngospasm that led to a dental injury","fontSize":9,"x":310.731,"y":303.5277999999998,"width":256.73400000000004,"height":9}]
[["page","lines",23],{"text":"during the expander surgery. None of these adverse events was","fontSize":9,"x":310.731,"y":314.5257999999998,"width":256.72500000000014,"height":9}]
[["page","lines",24],{"text":"related to the intervention of the study.","fontSize":9,"x":310.731,"y":325.52379999999977,"width":146.8692000000002,"height":9}]
[["page","lines",25],{"text":"Discussion","fontSize":10,"x":310.7245,"y":356.52680000000004,"width":47.47000000000003,"height":10}]
[["page","lines",26],{"text":"When conducting studies of this kind, power calculations are chal-","fontSize":9,"x":310.7245,"y":374.52680000000004,"width":256.73310000000043,"height":9}]
[["page","lines",27],{"text":"lenging and easily err. We aimed to include 10 patients more than we","fontSize":9,"x":310.7245,"y":385.5248,"width":256.70789999999994,"height":9}]
[["page","lines",28],{"text":"needed according to the calculation. Inclusion rate decreased over","fontSize":9,"x":310.7245,"y":396.5228,"width":256.7160000000002,"height":9}]
[["page","lines",29],{"text":"time, and we had more drop-outs than expected. The main reason of","fontSize":9,"x":310.7245,"y":407.5208,"width":256.7250000000002,"height":9}]
[["page","lines",30],{"text":"the decrease were increased availability of increased use of primary","fontSize":9,"x":310.7245,"y":418.5188,"width":256.72499999999997,"height":9}]
[["page","lines",31],{"text":"breast reconstruction. Nevertheless, the analyzes point in the same","fontSize":9,"x":310.7245,"y":429.5168,"width":256.69620000000015,"height":9}]
[["page","lines",32],{"text":"direction despite few patients. Not being able to blind the surgeon","fontSize":9,"x":310.7245,"y":440.5148,"width":256.6961999999999,"height":9}]
